From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Say where a new thread stops on this console.

GTA IV's hang is not graphics. The game waits on a DirectSound buffer's
notification positions; under that is waveOutOpen(WAVE_MAPPER), and under
that WINMM_StartDevicesThread, which creates a thread and waits on
{event, thread handle} forever (dlls/winmm/waveform.c:2377) -- the
"handles {f4, f8}, timeout (infinite)" that has been in every log today.

That thread never runs one guest instruction. With a probe in the WoW64
CPU backend, BTCpuThreadInit fires exactly once in a whole run, for the
main thread, and never for this one; only two thread ids appear in the
log at all. The thread object exists and has not died -- it is the
handle being waited on. So the host thread is wedged somewhere between
pthread_create and wow64's per-thread hook, and nothing in that stretch
says a word.

This is that stretch, four lines of it: the spawn and its stack, entry to
server_init_thread, the reply pipe and unix tid, and the suspend flag the
server answered with. Each one separates a different cause -- a thread
that never starts, one that cannot make its first server call, one the
server told to stay suspended.

⚠ ERR, not fprintf to stderr. ntdll's raw stderr reaches nothing here.
Not one "wine-ps5:" line has ever appeared in a session log -- not these,
and not this port's own: the fd-release switch report from 0870, the
WINE_PS5_WAIT_WATCHDOG banner, the slow-thread-start warning that exists
for exactly this situation. The sink ntdll installs takes Wine's debug
output, not libc's stderr. ERR arrives, and it arrives even from a thread
with no TEB -- that is how the SIGPROF fault reported itself as 0000.

⚠ Diagnostic only. There is a WINE_PS5_WAIT_WATCHDOG that covers some of
this already, but the launcher passes Wine no environment and this
console's environ is its own problem, so it has never once been on.
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
index e725c4d521..4443a98cc3 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
@@ -2437,12 +2437,25 @@ void server_init_thread( struct thread_data *data )
 
     data->pthread_id = pthread_self();
     pthread_setspecific( thread_data_key, data );
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* ⚠ DIAGNOSTIC: see spawn_thread in dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c. A 32-bit
+     * thread never reaches wow64, and nothing between pthread_create and
+     * BTCpuThreadInit says a word. These lines are that stretch. */
+    ERR( "wine-ps5: thread entered tid=%04x\n", (unsigned)data->tid );
+#endif
     if (data->ps5_spawn_us && ps5_now_us() - data->ps5_spawn_us > 100000)
         fprintf( stderr, "wine-ps5: slow thread start ms=%llu\n", (ps5_now_us() - data->ps5_spawn_us) / 1000 );
 
     reply_pipe = init_thread_pipe( data );
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    ERR( "wine-ps5: thread pipe tid=%04x reply=%d unix_tid=%d\n",
+             (unsigned)data->tid, reply_pipe, get_unix_tid() );
+#endif
 #ifdef WINE_INPROCESS_SERVER
     register_inprocess_thread( get_unix_tid() );
+#endif
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    ERR( "wine-ps5: thread registered tid=%04x\n", (unsigned)data->tid );
 #endif
     SERVER_START_REQ( init_thread )
     {
@@ -2455,6 +2468,10 @@ void server_init_thread( struct thread_data *data )
         data->suspend = reply->suspend;
     }
     SERVER_END_REQ;
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    ERR( "wine-ps5: thread init done tid=%04x suspend=%d\n",
+             (unsigned)data->tid, data->suspend );
+#endif
 #ifndef __PROSPERO__
     /* the server holds a duplicate of this pipe. On PS4 it holds this very
      * descriptor -- wine_server_send_fd hands it over rather than copying it --
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
index 0477c558ca..e81863931a 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
@@ -1349,6 +1349,18 @@ static NTSTATUS spawn_thread( struct thread_data *data )
         InterlockedDecrement( &nb_threads );
         status = STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
     }
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    /* ⚠ DIAGNOSTIC. A 32-bit thread this process creates never reaches wow64:
+     * BTCpuThreadInit fires once, for the main thread, and never again, while
+     * winmm's devices thread -- created here -- waits to be told it is ready
+     * and never is. The thread object exists and has not died, so the host
+     * thread is wedged somewhere between pthread_create and wow64's per-thread
+     * hook, and nothing in that stretch says a word. These four lines are that
+     * stretch; stderr from ntdll reaches the session log as "WINE <text>". */
+    ERR( "wine-ps5: spawn_thread tid=%04x status=%08x stack=%p+%zu\n",
+             (unsigned)data->tid, (unsigned)status, get_kernel_stack( data ),
+             (size_t)kernel_stack_size );
+#endif
     pthread_attr_destroy( &attr );
     pthread_sigmask( SIG_SETMASK, &sigset, NULL );
     return status;
